  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1204 AM MST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nThe long term period will be mainly dry with mild temperatures. \nExpect temps mainly in the M/U 60s each day, expect for Wednesday as \ntemps will only reach into the lower 60s across the plains. This \nbrief cooldown will be due to a cool front that will move across the \nregion late Tuesday, with cooler air coming into Tuesday night and \nWednesday. As the front goes by, it will be dry, but we will likely \nsee breezy conditions late Tuesday into Wednesday, with surface \nwinds decreasing and veering on Wednesday.\n\nBy very late in the period (early next week), shortwaves in advance \nof a large trough coming in from the Pacific may begin to impact the \ncontdvd region, bring a chance of rain and snow showers. Confidence \nis high that it will gradually get more unsettled next week, but the \nmagnitude of the unsettled weather still needs to be determined as \nthe long range guidance is not in agreement with intensity and \nlocation of the energy moving onshore. \\/Hodanish",
